From d05db934d9962b7060a7b3adb2ca9cacdbaef7e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude-brain <build@claude-brain.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:58:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] registry: add gpt-6.1-sol to the codex team/plus/pro catalogs

OpenAI released GPT-6.1 Sol on 2026-09-29 for Plus, Pro, Business,
Enterprise and Edu accounts in Codex. Upstream has not added it yet, and
claude-brain runs the proxy with --local-model, so a model that is absent
from the embedded catalog fails with 'unknown provider for model
gpt-6.1-sol' before reaching OpenAI.

Values follow the Codex model catalog served to a Business account on
2026-09-29: 272k context window, text and image input. Tier membership
matches gpt-6-astra (team, plus, pro, not free). The thinking levels stop
at max, as they do for astra; the Codex-only 'ultra' level is omitted.

Only models.json is touched: codex_client_models.json falls back to the
default template for an unknown id.
---
 internal/registry/models/models.json | 93 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 93 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/registry/models/models.json b/internal/registry/models/models.json
index 1ecca07c..2439325f 100644
